WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Requests rarely arrive as clean engineering tickets. They start in chat, email, meetings, or support conversations.

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
In Intake, an engineering lead captures the original message and connects it to the right project.

00:14.000 --> 00:25.000
AI proposes a clear title, summary, request type, and any questions that still need an answer. Nothing leaves the system yet.

00:25.000 --> 00:36.000
The lead reviews the proposal, adjusts the priority, chooses GitHub as the delivery target, and makes the final decision.

00:36.000 --> 00:45.000
Intake creates a real Issue from the approved snapshot, with a traceable link back to the original request.

00:45.000 --> 00:56.000
In Daily Planning, the lead assigns the Issue to Maya, chooses the morning slot, and plans three hours against the team's capacity.

00:56.000 --> 01:05.000
Intake keeps the request, decision, Issue, plan, and delivery evidence in one visible journey.

01:05.000 --> 01:12.000
When work is complete, the lead can accept it or return it for another pass.

01:12.000 --> 01:17.000
One request. One traceable workflow. Human judgment at every critical step.

01:17.000 --> 01:22.000
Intake is self-hosted, open source, and integrates with GitHub or GitLab.
